# Kotha GPT — Roadmap (prioritized, milestone-driven)

Objective: Build a production-capable, Bangla-first AI ecosystem focusing on practical impact, reproducibility, and fast iteration.

Guiding principles:

- Prioritize high-impact components first: dataset quality, tokenizer, inference/runtime, and developer UX.
- Keep scope incremental: ship a minimal working pipeline (tokenizer → small model → inference API → RAG) before scaling.
- Measure progress with objective success metrics (data coverage, eval scores, latency, cost).

Top-level milestones (priority order)

1. Foundation (0–6 weeks): dataset, tokenizer, minimal evals, reproducible data pipeline.
2. Fast inference (2–8 weeks): small 1–3B model experiments, optimized inference path (CPU/GPU), API server.
3. Instruction & Agents (4–12 weeks): SFT, simple agent tools, RAG integration.
4. Scale & Production (ongoing): large model training, quantization, orchestration, monitoring, security.

Quick wins / Immediate next actions (first 2 weeks)

- A1 — Audit and canonicalize datasets: produce a small validated Bangla corpus (10–50M tokens). Owner: @you. ETA: 1 week. Metric: token count, dedup rate.
- A2 — Finalize tokenizer & vocab: pick/configure a unigram/BPE tokenizer and publish vocab. Owner: `ml/tokenizer`. ETA: 3 days. Metric: token coverage, avg tokens per word.
- A3 — Stand up inference prototype: load a small model (1B) and expose a simple FastAPI endpoint in `services/api`. Owner: `services/api` team. ETA: 1 week. Metric: p95 latency < 500ms (local GPU), response correctness.
- A4 — Add CI task: dataset checks + tokenizer build + unit tests. Owner: `infra`. ETA: 3 days.

Roadmap structure (for each milestone)

- Goal: clear one-line goal.
- Deliverables: concrete artifacts (scripts, datasets, APIs, benchmarks).
- Success metrics: measurable acceptance criteria.
- Owners: placeholder teams or persons.
- Risks & mitigations: short bullet points.

Example: Foundation milestone

- Goal: Produce a validated Bangla training corpus and tokenizer.
- Deliverables:
 	- `data/processed/bangla-validated/` (sharded, deduped text)
 	- `ml/tokenizer/vocab.json` + tokenizer training script (`ml/tokenizer/train.py`)
 	- small evaluation set `evals/bangla-small.yaml`
- Success metrics:
 	- 10M+ clean tokens
 	- dedup rate < 3%
 	- tokenizer coverage > 99.5% on dev set
- Owners: Data (collection + cleaning), `ml/tokenizer` (tokenizer)
- Risks & mitigations:
 	- License/PII issues → enforce automated PII and license checks in pipeline.
 	- Low-quality sources → add source scoring and human spot checks.

Immediate checklist to add to repo

- [ ] Add `data/processed/README.md` describing final formats and shard structure.
- [ ] Add `ml/tokenizer/README.md` with training and evaluation commands.
- [ ] Create `services/api/quickstart.md` with a curl example for the prototype endpoint.
- [ ] Add lightweight `Makefile` targets: `make data-validate`, `make tokenizer-build`, `make serve-proto`.

Owners & roles (suggested)

- Data: collection, normalization, filters — Owner: `data/` team
- Tokenizer & token-vocab: Owner: `ml/tokenizer`
- Model experiments & training: Owner: `ml/pretrain` and `ml/sft`
- Inference & API: Owner: `services/api`, `inference/`
- Platform & infra: Owner: `infra/` (CI, monitoring, deployment)

Success metrics (project-wide)

- Data: token volume, dedup rate, PII detection rate
- Model: eval score on Bengali benchmark, hallucination rate
- System: latency p95, memory footprint, cost per 1k requests
- UX: time-to-first-successful-query for external devs

Suggested short-term timeline (12 weeks)

- Weeks 0–2: Foundation quick wins (A1–A4)
- Weeks 2–6: Inference prototype + tokenizer finalized + small model experiments
- Weeks 6–12: SFT/Instruction tuning on small model + RAG prototype

